# Preset deck generation

When the user asks to generate/rebuild a class deck:

1. Write a wipe-and-rebuild SQL migration (~10 sections × ~15 cards).
2. Always delete **old `tidbits` stubs** for that class as part of the wipe, not only `cards` / `deck_sections`:

```sql
DELETE FROM public.saved_tidbits
WHERE tidbit_id IN (SELECT id FROM public.tidbits WHERE category_id = '<slug>');

DELETE FROM public.tidbits
WHERE category_id = '<slug>';

DELETE FROM public.cards
WHERE deck_id = (SELECT id FROM public.decks WHERE slug = '<slug>');

DELETE FROM public.deck_sections
WHERE deck_id = (SELECT id FROM public.decks WHERE slug = '<slug>');
```

The study UI reads `cards`. `tidbits` is leftover from the old one-fact-per-row seed (`/api/tidbits` still reads it). Leaving those rows makes the Table Editor look like the deck was never rebuilt.

3. Apply the SQL to the live Tidbit Supabase project when MCP is available (including the tidbits delete).
4. Never use three consecutive apostrophes (`'''`) in card text; escape as `''`.
